cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pydivide: drainage divide networks in Python"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peifer
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9238-5072"
    email: peiferdaniel@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ATLAS-Topo/pydivide"
abstract: >-
  pydivide reimplements and extends the drainage-divide network
  algorithm of TopoToolbox 3 DIVIDEobj in Python. It removes the
  32-bit index ceiling that caps MATLAB FLOWobj at 4.29e9 cells,
  replaces the quadratic geometry and ordering stages with single-pass
  ones, and applies a deterministic local rule at diagonal flow
  crossings in place of an order-dependent merge cascade. It is
  the first module of ATLAS Topo.
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - geomorphology
  - drainage divide
  - digital elevation model
  - topographic analysis
  - TopoToolbox

references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Scherler
        given-names: Dirk
      - family-names: Schwanghart
        given-names: Wolfgang
    title: >-
      Drainage divide networks - Part 1: Identification and ordering in
      digital elevation models
    journal: "Earth Surface Dynamics"
    volume: 8
    start: 245
    end: 259
    year: 2020
    doi: "10.5194/esurf-8-245-2020"
    notes: >-
      The method pydivide reimplements. Cite this for the algorithm itself.
